{% block guide_content %}
<p class="guide-lead">A gender reveal is the moment you tell your loved ones whether the baby is a boy or a girl. Instead of simply announcing it, why not start with a game: everyone gives their opinion, then everybody discovers the answer at the same time?</p>

<h2>An interactive gender reveal</h2>
<p>The idea is to turn an announcement into a shared moment. Each guest votes (boy or girl) before the reveal, and the answer lands in front of everyone, or at a precise moment you choose. People laugh at the guesses, count the votes and congratulate those who called it right. It works just as well for a party as for an announcement to a family group chat from afar.</p>

<h2>How to set it up</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Create a game with the "gender" category only</strong>. Add the name or the date if you want more suspense.</li>
    <li><strong>Share the link</strong> by message, in your family group chat or on an invitation. Guests answer from their phone, without creating an account.</li>
    <li><strong>Follow the predictions</strong>: you can watch the boy/girl split build up without showing it to the players.</li>
    <li><strong>On the big day, enter the answer</strong>: the result appears on the reveal page, along with the list of guests who got it right.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Keeping the surprise until the birth?</h2>
<p>Nothing forces you to know the gender beforehand. The game stays open until you enter the answer: you can fill it in after the birth, and run predictions for date, weight and length alongside. For those categories, our tips are in the guide to the <a href="{{ path('app_guide', {'_locale': 'en', 'slug': 'baby-prediction-game'}) }}">baby prediction game</a>.</p>

<h2>Staging ideas</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Balloons</strong> to pop, filled with pink or blue confetti.</li>
    <li><strong>A cake</strong> whose inside reveals the colour at the first slice.</li>
    <li><strong>A box to open</strong> together, with a countdown.</li>
    <li><strong>A video call</strong> so faraway relatives live the reveal in real time.</li>
</ul>

<div class="guide-tip">
    <p><strong>Best avoided:</strong> pyrotechnic effects outdoors. Several fires have been started by reveals of this kind. Confetti and balloons are more than enough to make an impression, with no risk at all.</p>
</div>

<h2>When to open the votes</h2>
<p>The simplest approach is to open the game a few days before the party, or as soon as the pregnancy is announced, with a clear closing date. Each guest votes independently: they cannot see anyone else's prediction before the reveal, so nobody can be swayed by the majority.</p>

<h2>A keepsake to treasure</h2>
<p>When submitting a prediction, each guest can leave a short message for the parents-to-be. You will find all the votes and all the messages in one place, a lovely keepsake to read again later, funniest guesses included.</p>

<h2>Relatives far away are not left out</h2>
<p>The main advantage of an online game: grandparents abroad, cousins or childhood friends take part like everyone else, from a simple link, and learn the answer at the same time as you. To plan the wider celebration, see our guide to the <a href="{{ path('app_guide', {'_locale': 'en', 'slug': 'baby-shower-guessing-game'}) }}">baby shower guessing game</a>.</p>
